MountServiceIdler: Run the nightly storage trim on a device that is never idle

The storage maintenance job, which has vold trim /data and /cache, waits
for the device to be idle and charging. An Echo is wall powered with its
screen on, or has no screen, and most report no charging battery. The job
never ran: on the Echo Dot (3rd gen) the first manual run trimmed 1.3 GB
that had never been trimmed.

Drop the idle, charging and battery conditions. The job still runs once a
day at 3 AM. Regular trims tell the eMMC which blocks are free, which
lets it spread wear and keeps writes fast.

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/MountServiceIdler.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/MountServiceIdler.java
index 0f4c94bc..cc274e3d 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/MountServiceIdler.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/MountServiceIdler.java
@@ -111,9 +111,10 @@ public class MountServiceIdler extends JobService {
         }
 
         JobInfo.Builder builder = new JobInfo.Builder(MOUNT_JOB_ID, sIdleService);
-        builder.setRequiresDeviceIdle(true);
-        builder.setRequiresBatteryNotLow(true);
-        builder.setRequiresCharging(true);
+        // An Echo runs from the wall with its screen on or no screen at all.
+        // It is never idle the way a phone is and most report no charging
+        // battery, so with those conditions the nightly trim never ran. The
+        // trim takes a second or two, so run it at 3 AM regardless.
         builder.setMinimumLatency(nextScheduleTime);
         tm.schedule(builder.build());
     }
